Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.58,0:00:18.32,Default,Staff,0,0,0,,We have awaited your \Narrival, Wise Prince.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.41,0:00:23.29,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\b1\fnTimes New Roman\fs15\fade(238,434)\bord0.25\shad1.5\an2\pos(320,311.333)\c&HE8EEEF&\3c&H676C6B&\4c&H343C3B&}Ministry of Justice
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.51,0:00:29.42,Default,Viny,0,0,0,,It is truly an honor to meet you.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.93,0:00:33.97,Default,Viny,0,0,0,,I am Viny Aussie,\NVice Minister of Justice.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.25,0:00:33.88,nameplate,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fade(272,477)\pos(602,264)\c&HEBEFEF&\3c&H564240&}Viny Aussie\N{\fs13}Vice Minister of Justice
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.97,0:00:35.73,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,My number two, eh?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.73,0:00:38.57,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,He's young. Still on the rise, I'm sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.27,0:00:41.38,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,What are my duties?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.98,0:00:45.39,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Explain it to me.\NA rough outline will do.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.39,0:00:48.32,Default,Viny,0,0,0,,Of course. You have two primary duties.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.31,0:00:53.28,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs15\blur0.25\fnArial\bord0\shad1\c&HDCDCDC&\move(275.333,136.667,356,258,0,4951)}Meeres Empire
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.32,0:00:52.86,Default,Viny,0,0,0,,First is the coordination of all \Ncourthouses across the empire.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.27,0:00:59.10,Default,Viny,0,0,0,,Our ministry also tries many \Ncases that occur in the capital.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.48,0:01:02.59,Default,Viny,0,0,0,,And, as with the rebellion six years ago,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.05,0:01:08.23,Default,Viny,0,0,0,,it is customary for the ministry \Nor the emperor himself
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.69,0:01:13.08,Default,Viny,0,0,0,,to judge those who commit serious \Ncrimes such as insurrection.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.08,0:01:17.99,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,So in other words, the ministry also \Nfunctions as a common courthouse.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.33,0:01:19.73,Default,Viny,0,0,0,,That is correct.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.21,0:01:21.85,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Do you try cases, as well?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.06,0:01:24.68,Default,Viny,0,0,0,,Depending on the case.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.68,0:01:27.69,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,And how much do you receive in bribes?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.95,0:01:31.07,Default,Viny,0,0,0,,I-I do no such thing!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.69,0:01:34.30,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I'm not trying to force \Nyou into admitting guilt.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.73,0:01:36.98,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I only want to know the real story.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.98,0:01:39.50,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I'll forget as soon as I leave this room.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.50,0:01:41.25,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Just tell me the truth.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.80,0:01:46.46,Default,Viny,0,0,0,,I might have expected as much.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.89,0:01:48.98,Default,Viny,0,0,0,,I, personally, do not accept many bribes.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.46,0:01:52.93,Default,Viny,0,0,0,,A few hundred rean annually,\NI suppose.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.06,0:01:56.89,Default,Viny,0,0,0,,I have a rule, you see.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.33,0:02:00.54,Default,Viny,0,0,0,,Those beneath me accept at \Nleast ten times that much.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.54,0:02:01.97,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,What rule?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.37,0:02:04.59,Default,Viny,0,0,0,,I do not accept bribes \Nin cases of murder.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.88,0:02:05.97,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Why is that?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.23,0:02:07.68,Default,Viny,0,0,0,,It is too easily exposed.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.68,0:02:11.07,Default,Viny,0,0,0,,If the accuser bears a grudge, \NI could become a target for revenge,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.07,0:02:13.23,Default,Viny,0,0,0,,leading to irreparable damage.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.73,0:02:18.87,Default,Viny,0,0,0,,I accept bribes only in cases that \Ncould easily go in either direction.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.62,0:02:25.90,Default,Viny,0,0,0,,Your Highness?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.54,0:02:32.92,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Assuming you take 500 in a year, I'll \Ngive you 5,000, ten times that.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.92,0:02:35.51,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,You will not accept bribes while I'm here.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.71,0:02:41.47,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I want to live up to the emperor's \Nexpectations. Please help me do so.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.80,0:02:48.29,Default,Viny,0,0,0,,I can see why the emperor gave you \Nthe title of "the Wise" at age six
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.77,0:02:52.26,Default,Viny,0,0,0,,and appointed you \Nminister-prince of justice.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.08,0:02:55.02,Default,Viny,0,0,0,,I don't need extra money,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.79,0:02:57.72,Default,Viny,0,0,0,,and I will stop accepting bribes.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.72,0:03:01.24,Default,Viny,0,0,0,,Please allow me to work for Your \NHighness from this day forward.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.42,0:03:05.89,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,I should be suspicious of \Nulterior motives, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.12,0:03:09.39,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(0,493)\an4\c&HFFFFF9&\3c&HAC8F75&\4c&HA2775C&\shad1.5\bord0.5\blur1\fnTimes New Roman\b1\pos(122,122)}Name
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.12,0:03:09.39,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(0,493)\an4\c&HFFFFF9&\3c&HAC8F75&\4c&HA2775C&\shad1.5\bord0.5\blur1\fnTimes New Roman\b1\pos(186.667,122)}Noah Ararat  Minister-Prince of Justice
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.12,0:03:09.39,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(0,493)\an4\c&HFFFFF9&\3c&HAC8F75&\4c&HA2775C&\shad1.5\bord0.5\blur1\fnTimes New Roman\b1\pos(122,161.333)}Sex
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.12,0:03:09.39,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(0,493)\an4\c&HFFFFF9&\3c&HAC8F75&\4c&HA2775C&\shad1.5\bord0.5\blur1\fnTimes New Roman\b1\pos(184,161.333)}Male
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.12,0:03:09.39,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(0,493)\an4\c&HFFFFF9&\3c&HAC8F75&\4c&HA2775C&\shad1.5\bord0.5\blur1\fnTimes New Roman\b1\pos(122,198.667)}Level
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.12,0:03:09.39,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(0,493)\an4\c&HFFFFF9&\3c&HAC8F75&\4c&HA2775C&\shad1.5\bord0.5\blur1\fnTimes New Roman\b1\pos(356.667,321.334)}Fire
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.89,0:03:11.08,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs32\fad(507,0)\an4\c&HFFFFFC&\3c&HA27961&\4c&HA2775C&\shad0\bord2\blur3\fnTimes New Roman\b1\pos(199,171.334)}Strength
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.89,0:03:11.08,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs32\fad(507,0)\an4\c&HFFFFFC&\3c&HA27961&\4c&HA2775C&\shad0\bord2\blur3\fnTimes New Roman\b1\pos(199,256.001)}Stamina
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.89,0:03:11.08,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs32\fad(507,0)\an4\c&HFFFFFC&\3c&HA27961&\4c&HA2775C&\shad0\bord2\blur3\fnTimes New Roman\b1\pos(199,340.668)}Intelligence
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.12,0:03:13.53,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I'm counting on you, Viny.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.53,0:03:14.55,Default,Viny,0,0,0,,Of course.
Dialogue: 1,0:03:33.58,0:03:35.52,sign_generic,Title,0,0,0,,{\fade(109,0)\c&H4F7C81&\bord0\fnTimes New Roman\b1\fs10\pos(320,142.5)}Born Blessed, So I'll Obtain Ultimate Power
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.58,0:03:35.52,sign_generic,Title,0,0,0,,{\fade(109,0)\p1\bord2\c&H291505&\alpha&H255&\3c&H2986A5&\fscx87\pos(311,141.167)}m 0 0 l 235 0 l 225 8 l 235 15 l 18 15 l 30 8 l 18 0
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.34,0:05:04.23,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Thank you for arranging this grand \Ncelebration for me, Brother Oscar.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.23,0:05:08.12,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Well, I'm happy, too. \NAfter our brother Henry,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.24,0:05:10.70,nameplate,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fade(272,477)\pos(602,264)\c&HDDE6EC&\3c&H564240&}Oscar Ararat\N{\fs13}Eighth Prince
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.52,0:05:12.37,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,you're the second minister-prince in \Nall of the emperor's fifty-year reign.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.05,0:05:15.41,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Despite how it may seem, \NI quite like you.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.88,0:05:17.51,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Let me congratulate you.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.11,0:05:21.44,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,You aren't happy?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.90,0:05:28.47,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,It isn't that, but why did His Majesty \Nappoint us as minister-princes?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.85,0:05:30.97,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Probably because you're so dear to him.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.50,0:05:33.79,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,I can't completely rule that out.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.01,0:05:39.65,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,In Henry's case, he had the legitimate \Nreason of suppressing the rebellion.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.63,0:05:42.93,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,I don't have that kind of record,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.48,0:05:46.63,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,so maybe it's natural to conclude that \NHis Majesty is showing me favoritism.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.63,0:05:47.73,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,And yet...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.73,0:05:53.43,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Brother, you're aware the empire nearly\Ncollapsed at one point, are you not?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.81,0:05:54.96,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.18,0:06:02.59,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,It happened because of the empire's \Nsystem of choosing a crown prince to rule.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.87,0:06:06.74,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,Because the emperor's successor \Nis determined at birth,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.57,0:06:12.01,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,the princes who were not the crown \Nprince idled their lives away,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.01,0:06:15.10,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,and domestic stability \Nwas drastically shaken.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.47,0:06:17.43,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs13\blur0.25\fnArial\bord0\shad1.5\c&HDCDCDC&\move(336,285,336,372,0,1960)}Thirteenth Prince
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.47,0:06:19.35,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs13\blur0.25\fnArial\bord0\shad1.5\c&HDCDCDC&\move(533.333,189.333,533.333,361,0,3880)}Twelfth Prince
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.47,0:06:19.90,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs13\blur0.25\fnArial\bord0\shad1.5\c&HDCDCDC&\move(381.333,161.999,381.333,362,0,4430)}Eleventh Prince
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.47,0:06:22.15,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs13\blur0.25\fnArial\bord0\shad1.5\c&HDCDCDC&\move(535.333,63.333,535.333,362,0,6680)}Ninth Prince
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.47,0:06:22.94,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs13\blur0.25\fnArial\bord0\shad1.5\c&HDCDCDC&\move(409.333,27.999,409.333,362,0,7470)}Eighth Prince
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.47,0:06:20.02,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs13\blur0.25\fnArial\bord0\shad1.5\c&HDCDCDC&\move(103.333,157.333,103.333,360,0,4550)}Tenth Prince
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.47,0:06:23.07,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs13\blur0.25\fnArial\bord0\shad1.5\c&HDCDCDC&\move(117.333,21.333,117.333,360,0,7600)}Seventh Prince
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.60,0:06:23.98,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs13\blur0.25\fnArial\bord0\shad1.5\c&HDCDCDC&\move(266.667,-12.667,266.667,361,0,8380)}Imperial Castle
Dialogue: 1,0:06:15.77,0:06:21.12,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,Following introspection, the empire \Nnow grants every prince his own fief,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.10,0:06:25.94,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs13\blur0.25\fnArial\bord0\shad1.5\c&HDCDCDC&\move(542,-13.334,542,334.667,0,7827)}Sixth Prince
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.98,0:06:25.94,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs13\blur0.25\fnArial\bord0\shad1.5\c&HDCDCDC&\move(414,-14.667,414,298,0,6947)}Fifth Prince
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.35,0:06:25.94,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs13\blur0.25\fnArial\bord0\shad1.5\c&HDCDCDC&\move(127.333,-11.334,127.333,281.333,0,6577)}Fourth Prince
Dialogue: 1,0:06:21.61,0:06:25.09,italics,Narrator,0,0,0,,and ensures they get a proper education.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.69,0:06:25.94,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs13\blur0.25\fnArial\bord0\shad1.5\c&HDCDCDC&\move(527.333,-12,527.333,174,0,4237)}Third Prince
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.19,0:06:25.94,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs13\blur0.25\fnArial\bord0\shad1.5\c&HDCDCDC&\move(204,-12,204,153.333,0,3750)}First Prince
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.23,0:06:25.94,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs13\blur0.25\fnArial\bord0\shad1.5\c&HDCDCDC&\move(394.667,-12.667,394.667,153.333,0,3697)}Second Prince
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.94,0:06:28.19,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,But what does that have to do with this?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.87,0:06:33.57,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Don't you think appointing me minister \Ngoes beyond "an education"?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.21,0:06:35.36,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,You can't mean...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.37,0:06:44.24,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,he wants to make {\i1}you{\i0} crown prince?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.79,0:06:46.31,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I don't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.31,0:06:50.30,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,If he's merely doting on me, \Nthere's no problem, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.97,0:06:53.01,Default,Butler,0,0,0,,Your Highness...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.06,0:06:58.85,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Incredible. You were right.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.85,0:06:59.68,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Hmm?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.17,0:07:03.15,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I received a report from \Na eunuch I've bought off.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.40,0:07:05.16,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,The emperor intends
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.16,0:07:09.15,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,to name me minister-prince of finance \Nat tomorrow's morning assembly.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.38,0:07:12.65,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,It can't be...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.93,0:07:15.55,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,The emperor is making Albert...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:19.95,0:07:21.25,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,At any rate...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.53,0:07:25.77,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,today, we're here to celebrate \Nyou and toast your intuition.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.77,0:07:26.80,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.58,0:07:30.66,Default,Guys,0,0,0,,What's this?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.69,0:07:34.63,Default,Guys,0,0,0,,Stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.08,0:07:49.04,Default,Prime Minister,0,0,0,,I am told that 167 were \Narrested, including Keats.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.04,0:07:53.23,Default,Prime Minister,0,0,0,,They intended to pressure\NYour Majesty into abdicating and,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.23,0:07:56.31,Default,Prime Minister,0,0,0,,once you were deposed as emperor, have \Nthe crown prince assume the throne.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.08,0:08:00.32,Default,Prime Minister,0,0,0,,They confessed to the very \Nplot our intel indicated.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.09,0:08:07.85,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,He has been crown prince for\Nthirty years of my fifty-year reign.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.85,0:08:10.12,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I suppose he can wait no longer.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.12,0:08:15.37,Default,Prime Minister,0,0,0,,Bear in mind that there is no evidence \Nof the crown prince's involvement
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.37,0:08:17.34,Default,Prime Minister,0,0,0,,in this incident.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.68,0:08:21.23,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I am aware. I won't do \Nanything to Albert.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.76,0:08:25.27,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,This Keats man will be executed, \Nand that will be the end of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.89,0:08:32.48,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,What became of the incident with Oscar?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.48,0:08:37.12,Default,Prime Minister,0,0,0,,I have just sent out a eunuch who \Nis friends with His Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.12,0:08:40.18,Default,Prime Minister,0,0,0,,It would seem His Highness \Nwas aware of the situation.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.55,0:08:41.45,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Oh?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.45,0:08:44.49,Default,Prime Minister,0,0,0,,His Highness Noah was with him, as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.74,0:08:48.90,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Then it must have been Noah who \Ncaught on to my intentions.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.08,0:08:51.63,Default,Prime Minister,0,0,0,,According to the report...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.03,0:08:56.09,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Of course. Remarkable as ever, that Noah.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.72,0:09:00.60,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Gilbert is no good.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.02,0:09:02.73,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Albert is no good.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.73,0:09:07.12,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Who, then? Who is worthy \Nof succeeding me?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.12,0:09:10.55,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Henry? Oscar? Noah?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.51,0:09:20.25,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Any of them will do as long \Nas he can overcome my trial.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.83,0:09:26.58,sign_generic,Title,0,0,0,,{\fnTimes New Roman\bord0\b1\fade(522,640)\c&H00070B&\pos(320, 205)}Episode 7
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.83,0:09:26.58,sign_generic,Title,0,0,0,,{\fnTimes New Roman\bord0\b1\fade(522,640)\c&H00070B&\pos(320, 225)}The Emperor's Wishes
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.71,0:09:34.13,Default,Viny,0,0,0,,The aforementioned are the leader and \Naccomplices in the attempted insurrection.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.18,0:09:39.93,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,And of course they're all \Npeople close to Albert.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.65,0:09:45.74,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,His confidant, his former tutor,\Nhis knights...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.74,0:09:50.49,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Anyone would conclude that this was a \Nrevolt led by the crown prince's faction.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.49,0:09:52.81,Default,Viny,0,0,0,,What will you do?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.28,0:09:58.37,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,That's the natural reaction.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.76,0:10:01.72,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,As for whether Albert had \Na hand in this or not...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.64,0:10:07.48,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Under imperial law, if one of the \Nimperial family commits a crime,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.48,0:10:11.37,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,there are provisions that ensure \Ntheir penalty is light.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.76,0:10:13.74,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,But there is just one exception:
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.17,0:10:16.37,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,insurrection.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.32,0:10:19.85,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Any member of the imperial family \Nwho is involved in an insurrection
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.87,0:10:24.48,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,is to be cut in half at the waist, \Nbe they leader or accomplice.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.75,0:10:28.69,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,They face the same sentence if \Nthey are aware of the scheme
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.69,0:10:30.94,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,and fail to report it to the emperor.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.20,0:10:33.77,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Given how many of his \Npeople are involved,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.77,0:10:36.96,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,there's no way Albert \Ndidn't know about this.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.44,0:10:38.31,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.77,0:10:42.60,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,The crown prince's \Ninsurrection and execution
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.78,0:10:42.95,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\bord1.5\c&HE1E6E8&\3c&HD3CA81&\blur3\b1\fnTimes New Roman\pos(294,93.333)}Emperor
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.78,0:10:41.36,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fade(0,429)\bord1.5\fs15\c&HE1E6E8&\3c&HD3CA81&\blur3\b1\fnTimes New Roman\pos(158.667,209.333)}Crown Prince, Second Prince
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.78,0:10:41.36,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fade(0,429)\bord0.5\fs15\c&HE1E6E8&\3c&HD3CA81&\blur3\b1\fnTimes New Roman\pos(159.334,289.333)}Albert
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.78,0:10:42.95,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\bord1.5\fs15\c&HE1E6E8&\3c&HD3CA81&\blur3\b1\fnTimes New Roman\pos(479.333,218.666)}Third Prince
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.78,0:10:42.95,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs15\c&HE1E6E8&\3c&HD3CA81&\blur3\bord0.5\b1\fnTimes New Roman\pos(480.666,287.333)}Kiro
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.45,0:10:49.56,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,would be a massive scandal that shakes \Nthe very foundation of the empire.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.72,0:10:52.26,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,What has the emperor said?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.61,0:10:56.11,Default,Viny,0,0,0,,He said to state the relevant law,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.11,0:10:59.09,Default,Viny,0,0,0,,and to punish those involved accordingly.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.68,0:11:01.02,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.67,0:11:03.61,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I now understand the \Nemperor's intentions.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.48,0:11:08.56,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I will now pass judgment.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.55,0:11:18.99,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.91,0:11:23.67,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I have decided how to \Nsentence the insurgents.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.12,0:11:25.15,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Proceed.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.79,0:11:30.66,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,From among those who were arrested, the \Nleader will be cut in half at the waist,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.66,0:11:32.78,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,and the accomplices will be executed.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.07,0:11:36.29,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,The executions will be carried out\Nas soon as they are sentenced.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.25,0:11:41.82,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,The fact that he limited \Nit only to those arrested
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.82,0:11:45.93,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,must mean that he currently has no \Nintention of bringing Albert into this.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.41,0:11:50.31,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,That means only those on \Nthe list will be judged.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.28,0:11:53.04,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,I could postpone their deaths
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.04,0:11:56.18,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,until the day of the year when \Nall executions are carried out.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.02,0:12:02.91,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,But Albert's involvement could be revealed,\Nthrough a pardon or something similar.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.91,0:12:05.36,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,So I must execute them as soon as possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.17,0:12:08.93,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,This is all within the \Nbounds of imperial law.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.61,0:12:11.89,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Well done.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.51,0:12:13.66,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Cruz.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.66,0:12:14.62,Default,Cruz,0,0,0,,Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.62,0:12:16.75,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Noah has done well.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.14,0:12:20.43,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Add a thousand rean to his annual salary.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.43,0:12:24.39,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,This is not a feat worthy of a reward.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.77,0:12:28.40,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,He really didn't want to \Nget Albert involved in this.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.98,0:12:30.89,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Brilliant as usual, Noah.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.49,0:12:35.49,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,My hopes for you remain high. \NKeep up the good work.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.36,0:12:46.60,Default,Shirley,0,0,0,,Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.96,0:12:55.65,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Hey! What happened?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.61,0:12:57.83,Default,GuardB,0,0,0,,Your... Highness...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.83,0:13:02.83,Default,GuardB,0,0,0,,Intruders... still... inside...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.83,0:13:03.78,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Hey!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.83,0:13:07.61,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Send for reinforcements!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.61,0:13:09.77,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Ask my brother at the Ministry \Nof Military Affairs to—
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.77,0:13:11.71,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Wait... The timing of this...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.67,0:13:13.56,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.16,0:13:16.48,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Gather our allies!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.48,0:13:19.79,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Let no one inside or outside \Nthe mansion other than me,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.79,0:13:21.64,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,even the other princes!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.96,0:13:23.24,Default,Shirley,0,0,0,,Understood.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.65,0:13:33.83,Default,OfficialC,0,0,0,,Y-Your Highness...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.24,0:13:35.71,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,All officials, stand down!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:42.72,0:13:43.79,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Not good enough!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:46.63,0:13:47.92,Default,Black ClothesD,0,0,0,,Damn it!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.27,0:13:49.94,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I won't let you commit suicide.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.34,0:13:52.46,Default,Black ClothesE,0,0,0,,Hey! We're pulling out!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.78,0:14:05.70,Default,Black ClothesE,0,0,0,,Impossible!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.94,0:14:15.14,Default,Viny,0,0,0,,Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.82,0:14:21.28,Default,Viny,0,0,0,,I don't believe it... \NYou defeated them all?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.28,0:14:22.42,Default,Viny,0,0,0,,Incredible...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.81,0:14:23.91,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,What's the situation?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.32,0:14:27.00,Default,Viny,0,0,0,,You can see the casualties \Namong our guards.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.00,0:14:31.88,Default,Viny,0,0,0,,And all the insurgents were killed.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.82,0:14:34.09,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,All of them?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.76,0:14:37.35,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,They were silenced.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.80,0:14:42.29,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,In other words, these are Albert's...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.77,0:14:44.47,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,the crown prince's men.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.68,0:14:51.52,Default,Viny,0,0,0,,Your Highness?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.68,0:14:54.40,Default,Viny,0,0,0,,Your Highness! What are you...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.21,0:14:59.38,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,These four did this to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.38,0:15:04.04,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,What is the heaviest punishment \Nfor severely wounding a prince?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.90,0:15:10.00,Default,Viny,0,0,0,,Execution in all cases, \Nand by summary judgment.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.00,0:15:12.64,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Then do that immediately!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.64,0:15:13.67,Default,Viny,0,0,0,,Of course!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.88,0:15:31.37,Default,Viny,0,0,0,,The executions have been carried out.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.37,0:15:35.32,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Good. Now this whole matter is over.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.93,0:15:38.81,Default,Viny,0,0,0,,Your Highness never ceases to amaze.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.01,0:15:47.26,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,I swear... One misstep and the whole \Nempire would've been on the rocks.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.26,0:15:48.39,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Damned crown prince.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.16,0:15:54.92,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Pardon me.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.26,0:15:58.75,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Sorry to summon you here.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.75,0:16:02.80,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,You are wounded, no less. \NThere's no need for formality.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.40,0:16:04.98,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Thank you, Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.43,0:16:09.35,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I could not be more \Nashamed at my failure.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.11,0:16:13.97,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,No matter. You are not solely to blame.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.94,0:16:19.95,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Still, to think they wounded \Na man of your caliber.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.95,0:16:22.62,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Were they truly so capable?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.28,0:16:25.58,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,I figured he would ask that.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.58,0:16:27.66,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Given his intelligence network,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.10,0:16:32.34,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,he probably already knows that \NI gave myself this wound.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.04,0:16:34.55,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I believe that strength...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.25,0:16:39.07,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,is not solely dependent on \None's skill with the sword.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.45,0:16:41.69,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,No matter how talented one is,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.69,0:16:45.89,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,he can falter if his mental \Nfragility is taken advantage of.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:45.89,0:16:49.11,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I see. Truly, I have a fine son...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.11,0:16:53.61,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,no, a son I would be proud \Nto present to all.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.93,0:16:59.26,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,It appears he understands the amount \Nof thought I put into handling that.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.80,0:17:03.95,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I only wish all my sons were like you.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.79,0:17:09.73,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Can you walk with me?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.58,0:17:17.48,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Did you know, Noah,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.45,0:17:21.53,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,among emperors who come \Nto be known as great leaders,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.53,0:17:25.48,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,nine out of ten tarnish their \Nreputation later in life.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.71,0:17:29.10,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Is he talking about the\Ncrown prince's insurrection?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:31.73,0:17:35.84,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Our emperor led this nation into a golden \Nage like none it had known before.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.84,0:17:39.75,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,He will most certainly be described \Nas a great leader in history books.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.42,0:17:43.96,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,But if that insurrection \Nhad been successful,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.96,0:17:47.81,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,they would say he grew \Nsenile in his old age
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.47,0:17:50.49,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,and couldn't even control his own sons.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.61,0:17:55.92,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Clearly, the emperor no longer \Ntrusts the crown prince.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.33,0:17:58.46,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,The reason he won't do \Nanything about it now
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.16,0:18:01.67,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,is because the very act of \Nforsaking the crown prince
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.21,0:18:04.63,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,would tarnish his reputation \Nin his later years.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.91,0:18:10.65,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, if I may, \NI have a favor to ask.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.65,0:18:11.90,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.90,0:18:18.90,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,You appointed Henry, Oscar, \Nand myself minister-princes,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.36,0:18:21.65,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,but as that in itself is a first,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.14,0:18:24.94,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I fear some aspects of it will be handled \Npoorly somewhere down the line.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.36,0:18:31.20,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,So I would appreciate it if you could \Nappoint someone to coordinate all of us.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.53,0:18:34.45,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Are you asking for my \Nfirst prime minister?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.45,0:18:38.83,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,No, as an example, you could appoint \Nsomeone above the three of us
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.83,0:18:40.93,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,to bring order to all that we do.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:41.07,0:18:46.85,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\bord1\blur3\shad1\fs40\fade(925,1393)\fnTimes New Roman\b1\c&HFEFFFF&\3c&HA98B74&\4c&H8A6F60&\move(415,220,270,220,0,5780)}Prime Minister-Prince
Dialogue: 0,0:18:41.35,0:18:45.84,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I am proposing the establishment of a new \Nrole known as the prime minister-prince.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.40,0:18:53.94,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,And I would like His Highness the \NCrown Prince to fill that role.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.05,0:18:56.11,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Impossible.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.52,0:19:02.29,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Your wounds aren't healed yet.\NLeave for today.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.67,0:19:08.04,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,A crown prince of thirty years...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.54,0:19:13.03,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I can understand why my brother \Nwould begin to feel impatient.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.90,0:19:15.00,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,In which case...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.29,0:19:18.27,top,Noah,0,0,0,,Your Majesty would still have \Nthe final say in all decisions.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.69,0:19:22.97,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs40\fnTimes New Roman\b1\c&HFFFFFC&\3c&HAB8C73&\4c&H8A6F60&\bord1\blur3\shad1\fade(1090,0)\t(3384,5303,\fs28)\move(320,212,320,105,3384,5303))}Emperor
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.82,0:19:22.02,top,Noah,0,0,0,,You need only allow him to emulate you.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.05,0:19:22.97,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs32\fnTimes New Roman\b1\c&HFFFFFC&\3c&HAB8C73&\4c&H8A6F60&\bord1\blur3\shad1\fade(983,0)\t(0,1818,\fs40)\move(320,270,320,304.667,0,1818)}Prime Minister-Prince
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.97,0:19:26.93,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,But he would still rank above \Nthe ministers, would he not?
Dialogue: 1,0:19:26.93,0:19:30.15,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,What if the prime minister \Ndismisses an important matter
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.93,0:19:32.89,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs10\fnTimes New Roman\c&HFFFEFD&\4c&HA17665&\bord0.5\shad1.25\b1\blur0.25\move(206.667,80,206.667,343.333,0,5960)\3c&HBBA08F&}Minister-Prince\Nof Finance
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.93,0:19:32.89,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs10\fnTimes New Roman\c&HFFFEFD&\4c&HA17665&\bord0.5\shad1.25\b1\blur0.25\move(318,80,318,343.333,0,5960)\3c&HBBA08F&}Minister-Prince\Nof Justice
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.93,0:19:32.89,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs10\fnTimes New Roman\c&HFFFEFD&\4c&HA17665&\bord0.5\shad1.25\b1\blur0.25\move(427,80,427,343.333,0,5960)\3c&HBBA08F&}Minister-Prince\Nof Military Affairs
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.95,0:19:32.89,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs32\fnTimes New Roman\c&HFFFEFD&\4c&HA17665&\bord0.5\shad1.25\b1\blur0.25\move(320,-26,320,231.333,0,5940)\3c&HBBA08F&}Prime Minister-Prince
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.15,0:19:32.54,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,and it never reaches me at all?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.25,0:19:32.89,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs15\fnTimes New Roman\c&HFFFEFD&\4c&HA17665&\bord0.5\shad1.25\b1\blur0.25\3c&HBBA08F&\move(498,-30,498,88.333,0,2640)}(Final Say)
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.25,0:19:32.89,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs32\fnTimes New Roman\c&HFFFEFD&\4c&HA17665&\bord0.5\shad1.25\b1\blur0.25\3c&HBBA08F&\move(320,-30,320,81.333,0,2640)}Emperor
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.89,0:19:34.99,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,To prevent that,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.99,0:19:39.20,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,each minister-prince will have the \Nright to file a direct appeal.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.19,0:19:46.66,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs10\fnTimes New Roman\c&HFFFEFD&\4c&HA17665&\bord0.5\shad1.25\b1\blur0.25\move(206.667,80,206.667,343.333,0,7470)\3c&HBBA08F&}Minister-Prince\Nof Finance
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.19,0:19:46.66,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs10\fnTimes New Roman\c&HFFFEFD&\4c&HA17665&\bord0.5\shad1.25\b1\blur0.25\move(318,80,318,343.333,0,7470)\3c&HBBA08F&}Minister-Prince\Nof Justice
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.19,0:19:46.66,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs10\fnTimes New Roman\c&HFFFEFD&\4c&HA17665&\bord0.5\shad1.25\b1\blur0.25\move(427,80,427,343.333,0,7470)\3c&HBBA08F&}Minister-Prince\Nof Military Affairs
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.21,0:19:46.66,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs32\fnTimes New Roman\c&HFFFEFD&\4c&HA17665&\bord0.5\shad1.25\b1\blur0.25\move(320,-26,320,231.333,0,7433)\3c&HBBA08F&}Prime Minister-Prince
Dialogue: 1,0:19:39.56,0:19:42.43,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,If all of us feel equally \Nstrongly about the matter,
Dialogue: 1,0:19:42.43,0:19:45.85,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,we can bypass the prime minister \Nand appeal directly to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.32,0:19:46.66,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fade(529,0)\fs15\fnTimes New Roman\c&HFFFEFD&\4c&HA17665&\bord0.5\shad1.25\b1\blur0.25\move(77.333,190,77.333,305,0,3323)\3c&HBBA08F&}(Can Directly\NAppeal)
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.32,0:19:46.66,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fade(529,0)\fs15\fnTimes New Roman\c&HFFFEFD&\4c&HA17665&\bord0.5\shad1.25\b1\blur0.25\move(492,-7.333,492,87,112,3323)\3c&HBBA08F&}(Final Say)
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.34,0:19:46.66,sign_generic,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fs32\fnTimes New Roman\c&HFFFEFD&\4c&HA17665&\bord0.5\shad1.25\b1\blur0.25\move(320,-30,320,231.333,0,7433)\3c&HBBA08F&}Emperor
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.13,0:19:53.03,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,That prevents the crown prince \Nfrom holding any actual power.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.03,0:19:58.19,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,It doesn't matter if the prime \Nminister-prince's role has any substance.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.19,0:20:00.24,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,It will be no more than a title.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:04.24,0:20:05.87,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Remarkable.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:09.08,0:20:13.47,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,You are right. If that will \Nwork, it is the best choice.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.47,0:20:16.37,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Thank you for your counsel, Noah.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.79,0:20:19.08,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Consider it delivered to the throne.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:19.56,0:20:21.26,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,I am most grateful.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.59,0:20:30.43,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,It truly is a shame you \Nweren't born sooner.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.83,0:20:34.29,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,He understood my proposal instantly.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:34.69,0:20:37.33,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,He is truly worthy of being \Ncalled a great leader.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.08,0:20:41.03,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Preventing the tarnishing of \Nhis reputation in his old age
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.72,0:20:45.02,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,will be the best way to ensure his \Npeople can live peaceful lives.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.64,0:20:51.97,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I must reward you.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.81,0:20:56.16,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Money is not a sufficient \Nreward for such a proposal.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:56.16,0:20:57.21,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Cruz.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.21,0:20:58.10,Default,Cruz,0,0,0,,Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.71,0:21:02.53,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,We're going to the vault.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:21.63,0:21:26.09,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,It was by your own judgment that \Nyou discovered that ring, correct?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.09,0:21:27.13,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:27.49,0:21:29.65,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,I wish to see that judgment in action.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.65,0:21:32.20,Default,Emperor,0,0,0,,Choose any one item you like.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.20,0:21:33.79,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,Thank you, Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:39.20,0:21:41.01,italics,Noah,0,0,0,,Search, Leviathan.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:52.29,0:21:53.52,Default,Noah,0,0,0,,This one?
